id: pm-nl60tbxzkjwp
title: "GH-1532: preserve every tracker cache exclusion when nested init shares a repository"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1532 reproduces nested pm init replacing the one managed runtime-cache fence, leaving enclosing tracker caches unignored. Live SDK reproduction confirms outer cache becomes unignored while nested cache is ignored. Preserve existing tracker rules and unrelated user content, support either init order, and keep every tracker eval-queries.json version controllable. Merge-attribute preservation was not broken in the independent issue reproduction and must remain covered."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk","gh:1532",gitignore,init,multi-tracker
created_at: "2026-10-21T11:44:24.626Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T13:38:42.929Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T13:38:42.088Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T13:38:42.088Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Outer and nested trackers keep runtime/search/locks/transactions/checkpoints excluded in either initialization order; repeated initialization is byte-idempotent; unrelated ignore rules remain intact; curated eval queries remain trackable; both merge-attribute scopes remain effective
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: 90
severity: high
resolution: "Preserve tracker-specific cache rules, user bytes and unmatched prefixes through a single forward fence scan, retaining sibling scopes and repeated-init idempotence."
expected_result: Both initialization orders and malformed managed markers preserve every intended scope and remain bounded and byte-idempotent.
actual_result: "All linked commands pass, including4000 unmatched markers, real Git scope controls and orphan/CRLF fences. The prior idempotence failure is reproduced and fixed; public SDK measurements are linear at tested sizes. Revised exact-head CI and bot review remain mandatory before merge."
affected_version: 2026.10.21
component: sdk/workspace
